{"id": "b01", "tier": "T1", "kind": "sql", "turns": ["List the customers who live in Delhi."], "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "temperature": 0.0, "prompt_hash": "637813813df8", "schema_hash": "cace08063546", "commit": "f6e44c0", "ran_at": "2026-09-24T06:00:42+00:00", "answer": "The customers living in Delhi are Kabir Singh (kabir.singh@example.com), Nikhil Verma (nikhil.verma@example.com) and Karan Malhotra (karan.malhotra@example.com).", "sql": "SELECT * FROM customers WHERE city = 'Delhi' LIMIT 100", "columns": ["id", "name", "email", "city", "signup_date"], "rows_sample": [[5, "Kabir Singh", "kabir.singh@example.com", "Delhi", "2024-01-09"], [11, "Nikhil Verma", "nikhil.verma@example.com", "Delhi", "2024-04-19"], [15, "Karan Malhotra", "karan.malhotra@example.com", "Delhi", "2024-06-27"]], "row_count": 3, "truncated": false, "error": null, "out_of_scope": false, "checks": {"ref_row_count": 3, "got_row_count": 3, "exact_match": false, "projection_match": true, "pass": true}, "llm_calls": 2, "input_tokens": 841, "output_tokens": 302, "latency_s": 0.92, "model_reported": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": "ok"}
{"id": "b02", "tier": "T2", "kind": "sql", "turns": ["What is the total revenue?"], "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "temperature": 0.0, "prompt_hash": "637813813df8", "schema_hash": "cace08063546", "commit": "f6e44c0", "ran_at": "2026-09-24T06:00:57+00:00", "answer": "The total revenue is Rs 183,530.", "sql": "SELECT SUM(oi.unit_price * oi.quantity) AS total_revenue FROM order_items oi JOIN orders o ON oi.order_id = o.id WHERE o.status <> 'cancelled'", "columns": ["total_revenue"], "rows_sample": [[183530.0]], "row_count": 1, "truncated": false, "error": null, "out_of_scope": false, "checks": {"ref_row_count": 1, "got_row_count": 1, "exact_match": true, "projection_match": true, "pass": true}, "llm_calls": 2, "input_tokens": 758, "output_tokens": 219, "latency_s": 1.344, "model_reported": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": "ok"}
{"id": "b03", "tier": "T3", "kind": "sql", "turns": ["Show each order ID with the name of the customer who placed it."], "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "temperature": 0.0, "prompt_hash": "637813813df8", "schema_hash": "cace08063546", "commit": "f6e44c0", "ran_at": "2026-09-24T06:01:26+00:00", "answer": "The result lists each order ID together with the customer who placed it, showing the first 20 of 30 rows (e.g., orders 1, 5 and 18 belong to Aarav Sharma; 3, 14 and 28 to Diya Patel; 2 and 11 to Rohan Mehta; 7 and 22 to Ananya Iyer; 4 and 25 to Kabir Singh; 9 and 30 to Ishita Rao; 6 and 27 to Vikram Nair; 12 and 13 to Meera Joshi; 8 to Arjun Reddy; 16 to Sara Khan).", "sql": "SELECT orders.id AS order_id, customers.name AS customer_name FROM orders JOIN customers ON orders.customer_id = customers.id LIMIT 100", "columns": ["order_id", "customer_name"], "rows_sample": [[1, "Aarav Sharma"], [5, "Aarav Sharma"], [18, "Aarav Sharma"], [3, "Diya Patel"], [14, "Diya Patel"], [28, "Diya Patel"], [2, "Rohan Mehta"], [11, "Rohan Mehta"], [7, "Ananya Iyer"], [22, "Ananya Iyer"], [4, "Kabir Singh"], [25, "Kabir Singh"], [9, "Ishita Rao"], [30, "Ishita Rao"], [6, "Vikram Nair"], [27, "Vikram Nair"], [12, "Meera Joshi"], [13, "Meera Joshi"], [8, "Arjun Reddy"], [16, "Sara Khan"], [10, "Nikhil Verma"], [29, "Nikhil Verma"], [19, "Pooja Desai"], [21, "Riya Kapoor"], [15, "Karan Malhotra"], [23, "Tanvi Shah"], [17, "Dev Chauhan"], [26, "Neha Gupta"], [20, "Siddharth Menon"], [24, "Aisha Ali"]], "row_count": 30, "truncated": false, "error": null, "out_of_scope": false, "checks": {"ref_row_count": 30, "got_row_count": 30, "exact_match": true, "projection_match": true, "pass": true}, "llm_calls": 2, "input_tokens": 931, "output_tokens": 514, "latency_s": 1.44, "model_reported": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": "ok"}
{"id": "b04", "tier": "T4", "kind": "sql", "turns": ["Which product categories appear in more than 8 orders?"], "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "temperature": 0.0, "prompt_hash": "637813813df8", "schema_hash": "cace08063546", "commit": "f6e44c0", "ran_at": "2026-09-24T06:01:56+00:00", "answer": "The categories that appear in more than 8 orders are **Accessories** and **Electronics**.", "sql": "SELECT p.category FROM order_items oi JOIN products p ON oi.product_id = p.id JOIN orders o ON oi.order_id = o.id WHERE o.status <> 'cancelled' GROUP BY p.category HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT oi.order_id) > 8 LIMIT 100", "columns": ["category"], "rows_sample": [["Accessories"], ["Electronics"]], "row_count": 2, "truncated": false, "error": null, "out_of_scope": false, "checks": {"ref_row_count": 2, "got_row_count": 2, "exact_match": true, "projection_match": true, "pass": true}, "llm_calls": 2, "input_tokens": 766, "output_tokens": 276, "latency_s": 0.963, "model_reported": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": "ok"}
{"id": "b05", "tier": "T5", "kind": "sql", "turns": ["How many orders were placed each month in 2024?"], "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "temperature": 0.0, "prompt_hash": "637813813df8", "schema_hash": "cace08063546", "commit": "f6e44c0", "ran_at": "2026-09-24T06:02:25+00:00", "answer": "In 2024, the monthly order counts were: Jan 2, Feb 2, Mar 3, Apr 2, May 1, Jun 2, Jul 2, Aug 1, Sep 2, Oct 1, Nov 2, Dec 2.", "sql": "SELECT strftime('%Y-%m', order_date) AS month, COUNT(*) AS order_count FROM orders WHERE status != 'cancelled' AND order_date BETWEEN '2024-01-01' AND '2024-12-31' GROUP BY month ORDER BY month LIMIT 100", "columns": ["month", "order_count"], "rows_sample": [["2024-01", 2], ["2024-02", 2], ["2024-03", 3], ["2024-04", 2], ["2024-05", 1], ["2024-06", 2], ["2024-07", 2], ["2024-08", 1], ["2024-09", 2], ["2024-10", 1], ["2024-11", 2], ["2024-12", 2]], "row_count": 12, "truncated": false, "error": null, "out_of_scope": false, "checks": {"ref_row_count": 12, "got_row_count": 12, "exact_match": false, "projection_match": false, "pass": false}, "llm_calls": 2, "input_tokens": 862, "output_tokens": 362, "latency_s": 1.254, "model_reported": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": "ok"}
{"id": "b06", "tier": "T6", "kind": "sql", "turns": ["What are the top 3 products by units sold?"], "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "temperature": 0.0, "prompt_hash": "637813813df8", "schema_hash": "cace08063546", "commit": "f6e44c0", "ran_at": "2026-09-24T06:02:54+00:00", "answer": "The top three products by units sold are Notebook Set (11 units), Gel Pen Pack (9 units) and Wireless Mouse (7 units).", "sql": "SELECT p.name, SUM(oi.quantity) AS total_units\nFROM order_items oi\nJOIN orders o ON oi.order_id = o.id\nJOIN products p ON oi.product_id = p.id\nWHERE o.status != 'cancelled'\nGROUP BY p.id, p.name\nORDER BY total_units DESC\nLIMIT 3", "columns": ["name", "total_units"], "rows_sample": [["Notebook Set", 11], ["Gel Pen Pack", 9], ["Wireless Mouse", 7]], "row_count": 3, "truncated": false, "error": null, "out_of_scope": false, "checks": {"ref_row_count": 3, "got_row_count": 3, "exact_match": true, "projection_match": true, "pass": true}, "llm_calls": 2, "input_tokens": 783, "output_tokens": 307, "latency_s": 1.491, "model_reported": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": "ok"}
{"id": "b07", "tier": "T7", "kind": "sql", "turns": ["What percentage of total revenue does each customer account for?"], "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "temperature": 0.0, "prompt_hash": "637813813df8", "schema_hash": "cace08063546", "commit": "f6e44c0", "ran_at": "2026-09-24T06:03:24+00:00", "answer": "Vikram Nair accounts for the largest share at 18.47% of total revenue, followed by Ananya Iyer 15.69%, Dev Chauhan 11.99%, Pooja Desai 9.81%, Rohan Mehta 9.53%, Diya Patel 5.5%, Aarav Sharma 4.79%, Nikhil Verma 4.57%, Kabir Singh 3.38%, Riya Kapoor 2.34%, Ishita Rao 2.18%, Karan Malhotra 2.15%, Arjun Reddy 1.8%, Sara Khan 1.8%, Aisha Ali 1.53%, Siddharth Menon 1.31%, Tanvi Shah 1.19%, Meera Joshi 1.11% and Neha Gupta 0.87%.", "sql": "SELECT c.id, c.name, ROUND(SUM(oi.unit_price * oi.quantity) * 100.0 / (SELECT SUM(oi2.unit_price * oi2.quantity) FROM orders o2 JOIN order_items oi2 ON oi2.order_id = o2.id WHERE o2.status <> 'cancelled'), 2) AS revenue_pct FROM customers c JOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.id AND o.status <> 'cancelled' JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.id GROUP BY c.id, c.name HAVING SUM(oi.unit_price * oi.quantity) > 0 ORDER BY revenue_pct DESC LIMIT 100", "columns": ["id", "name", "revenue_pct"], "rows_sample": [[7, "Vikram Nair", 18.47], [4, "Ananya Iyer", 15.69], [17, "Dev Chauhan", 11.99], [12, "Pooja Desai", 9.81], [3, "Rohan Mehta", 9.53], [2, "Diya Patel", 5.5], [1, "Aarav Sharma", 4.79], [11, "Nikhil Verma", 4.57], [5, "Kabir Singh", 3.38], [14, "Riya Kapoor", 2.34], [6, "Ishita Rao", 2.18], [15, "Karan Malhotra", 2.15], [9, "Arjun Reddy", 1.8], [10, "Sara Khan", 1.8], [20, "Aisha Ali", 1.53], [19, "Siddharth Menon", 1.31], [16, "Tanvi Shah", 1.19], [8, "Meera Joshi", 1.11], [18, "Neha Gupta", 0.87]], "row_count": 19, "truncated": false, "error": null, "out_of_scope": false, "checks": {"ref_row_count": 19, "got_row_count": 19, "exact_match": false, "projection_match": true, "pass": true}, "llm_calls": 2, "input_tokens": 987, "output_tokens": 756, "latency_s": 2.277, "model_reported": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": "ok"}
{"id": "b08", "tier": "T8", "kind": "clarify", "turns": ["Who are the best customers?"], "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "temperature": 0.0, "prompt_hash": "637813813df8", "schema_hash": "cace08063546", "commit": "f6e44c0", "ran_at": "2026-09-24T06:03:54+00:00", "answer": "The best customers are Vikram Nair (Rs 33,895), Ananya Iyer (Rs 28,796), Dev Chauhan (Rs 21,999), Pooja Desai (Rs 17,998), Rohan Mehta (Rs 17,498), Diya Patel (Rs 10,094), Aarav Sharma (Rs 8,792), Nikhil Verma (Rs 8,396), Kabir Singh (Rs 6,197) and Riya Kapoor (Rs 4,298).", "sql": "SELECT c.id, c.name, c.email, SUM(oi.unit_price * oi.quantity) AS total_spent\nFROM customers c\nJOIN orders o ON c.id = o.customer_id AND o.status <> 'cancelled'\nJOIN order_items oi ON o.id = oi.order_id\nGROUP BY c.id, c.name, c.email\nORDER BY total_spent DESC\nLIMIT 10", "columns": ["id", "name", "email", "total_spent"], "rows_sample": [[7, "Vikram Nair", "vikram.nair@example.com", 33895.0], [4, "Ananya Iyer", "ananya.iyer@example.com", 28796.0], [17, "Dev Chauhan", "dev.chauhan@example.com", 21999.0], [12, "Pooja Desai", "pooja.desai@example.com", 17998.0], [3, "Rohan Mehta", "rohan.mehta@example.com", 17498.0], [2, "Diya Patel", "diya.patel@example.com", 10094.0], [1, "Aarav Sharma", "aarav.sharma@example.com", 8792.0], [11, "Nikhil Verma", "nikhil.verma@example.com", 8396.0], [5, "Kabir Singh", "kabir.singh@example.com", 6197.0], [14, "Riya Kapoor", "riya.kapoor@example.com", 4298.0]], "row_count": 10, "truncated": false, "error": null, "out_of_scope": false, "checks": {"pass": null}, "llm_calls": 2, "input_tokens": 959, "output_tokens": 496, "latency_s": 2.097, "model_reported": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": "ok"}
